        }
      ],
      "message": "wallet: return an error when wallet setup throws\n\nSetting up an external signer wallet throws std::runtime_error when the\nsigner fails, for example when it returns an invalid descriptor.\nCreateWallet() didn't catch it. Over RPC this became a generic -1\nerror, but the GUI creates wallets on a worker thread with no handler,\nso bitcoin-qt aborted.\n\nCatch std::runtime_error around CWallet::CreateNew(), as\nLoadWalletInternal() does when loading, and report it as a normal\ncreation failure. bitcoin-qt now shows its \"Create wallet failed\"\ndialog, and createwallet returns RPC_WALLET_ERROR (-4) instead of -1.\n\nUpdate the affected wallet_signer.py error codes, and add a unit test\nthat creates the wallet through the wallet loader, as the GUI does.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "zerog975",
        "email": "zerog9751@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-05T01:52:14Z"
      },
