        }
      ],
      "message": "wallet: remove the files of a failed creation\n\nCreateWallet() creates the wallet directory and its database\n(wallet.dat) before setting up the wallet. If setup then fails, they\nare left behind and the name can't be used again: the next attempt\nfails with \"Database already exists\". This happens for any setup\nfailure, over RPC as well as in the GUI.\n\nNote what exists before the database is created. On failure, remove\nthe database files only if wallet.dat is new, and the directory only\nif it is new and empty, as RestoreWallet() does. Use the non-throwing\nfs::remove() overloads, as the GUI does not catch exceptions here.\n\nExtend the unit test to retry the same name, add one for a failure\nthat doesn't throw, and check in wallet_signer.py that a directory and\nfiles that already existed are kept.",
      "committer": {
